* The weekly check was re-run under the new rules: **45 suggestions offered, 0 refused,
  0 need a look** (was *0 offered, 40 refused, 4 need a look*), so the owner's Games page no
  longer shows refusal reasons written by the retired licence rule.

**Still unproven after that work:** a game has never been **played** by a person on the Pi (no
phone sign-in, no save kept on the box). A headless Chromium on the Mac has *drawn* two of the
shelf's games from the box's own files — `2048-gb` (Game Boy) and `Apotris` (Game Boy Advance,
mgba) — and `getState()` returned 35,056 B and 430,168 B respectively (§18.2), so the serving
path is proved; the hands are not. The 23 files were fetched from the box's own
internet route and the carried-file path (`--seed --from-dir`) has only been proved in tests,
**SNES and Genesis have no catalogue entries at all** (a game for those consoles is hand-carried
with `--import`), and the first real cold boot into broadcast mode has not happened yet.
4. **The two fixes found after the deploy are now on the box** (`--only 60-portal,95-backup`, 25 Oct, §8.12a *After the deploy*): **Latest copy** reads the adopted `ark-backup-20261025-093643` (`pi:pi 700`) and `/files` no longer offers the leftover, but the *sentences themselves* have still not been seen in a browser — **What is working** has not been read on a screen by a human. (The account **is** claimed now: set up through the real `/admin/setup` door on the loopback listener on 25 Oct 2026, `must_change = 0`, and the page answers 200 with its own title — log §16.7. What is still missing is a person looking at it.) While the ghost `e2e-drop-test.epub` record is there `/api/ready` answers 503 `blocking: ["File Box"]`; deleting it on **Community → Shared files** is what returns the box to 200, and nobody has tapped it yet.

**Executed once, on 25 Oct 2026, by the deploy — no longer blind spots:**

* `60-portal.sh`'s `/api/ready` branch ran (it accepted 200 on the box) and its
  first-shelf seed branch ran; `65-admin.sh`'s `:8445` proof ran (200 + `/admin`
  404 + 400 on plain HTTP); `70-network.sh`'s timer branch ran (`ark-net-watch.timer`
  `enabled`+`active`); `95-backup.sh` ran; `90-verify.sh`'s readiness, timer/pin,
  game/player and backup blocks all ran.
* `ark-arcade --import` ran on the box for the first time (25 Oct, §18.4): a carried
  Game Boy file went on as a new game, served its ROM and drew its page — and giving
  the same file a third time exposed the missing fingerprint (revision 2 of an
